 "notModeled": [
  "charge-integrating analog front end (IN1, IN2, dual A/B integrators, external CAP pins, VREF, RANGE2-RANGE0 full-scale selection, TEST charge injection): the output is always the 0-input code 0000 0001 0000 0000 0000 (Table VIII: straight binary with a built-in offset of about 0.4 % FS), written literally in the frame for both inputs",
  "CONV: in the device every CONV transition (both edges) ends an integration and DVALID goes low t7 = 4212 CLK periods later; the model starts a conversion only on the CONV rising edge (convst edge \"rise\"), so it reports data every other transition",
  "continuous / non-continuous (ncont) integration state machine (Figures 10-19), the power-up ncont states and the CLK-synchronised m/r/az cycle: conversion time is fixed at t7 = 421.2 us (CLK = 10 MHz, DDC112U/Y); DDC112UK/YK at CLK = 15 MHz take 280.8 us",
  "CLK (system clock) is not used by the model; the conversion time assumes the nominal 10 MHz",
  "daisy-chain: after the 40 data bits the device shifts the DIN bits out on DOUT (Figure 20); the model shifts zeros",
  "DVALID goes high t19 = 30 ns after DXMIT falls (modeled as cleared at the DXMIT falling edge)",
  "timing: tValid t21 = 30 ns max, tOut t22B = 30 ns max (DDC112U/Y; t22A 25 ns for UK/YK), tFloat t23 = 30 ns (typical, the only value given)"
 ],
